ent-MobRotHungry = hungry
    .desc = A swollen carcass with sinewy fists and a sunken, festering face.
ent-RotNodule = rot nodule
    .desc = A living nursery of rot. Larvae stir among its roots.
ent-MobRotLarva = rot larva
    .desc = A pale, ravenous larva. Keep it away from bodies.
ent-RotInfectedVine = infected vine
    .desc = Thick strands of rot that catch the legs of passing creatures.
ent-RotMoldVine = moldy vine
    .desc = A damp carpet of mold that nourishes creatures born of the rot.
rot-larva-satiety = Satiety: {$current}/{$maximum}.
rot-larva-sated = The larva has pupated. A new creature stirs beneath its thick casing.
rot-pupa-name = rot pupa

ent-MobRotSated = sated
    .desc = A towering, emaciated silhouette. Something shifts beneath its loose, waxy skin.
rot-hungry-threat = You sense a threat: this humanoid is armed or has already shown aggression.
ghost-role-rot-hungry-name = Hungry
ghost-role-rot-hungry-description = A ferocious guardian of the rot colony, hunting those who could threaten it.
ghost-role-rot-hungry-rules =
    You are [color={ role-type-team-antagonist-color }][bold]Hungry[/bold][/color], a guardian of the rot colony.
    Your [color=green]allies[/color] are other Hungry, Sated, rot carriers and larvae.
    Your task is to [bold]protect your birthplace, rot creatures and their colonies[/bold]. Bring the bodies of your kills to rot nodules to feed their larvae.
    Your [color=red]targets[/color] are humanoids holding weapons or items usable as melee weapons, and humanoids who have attacked anyone or anything. Once a hunt begins, you may kill your prey even if they drop their weapon.
    You are [color=red][bold]FORBIDDEN[/bold][/color] from attacking peaceful, unarmed creatures who have shown no aggression, or harming allies and rot colonies.
    You do not remember your previous life or anything you learned while you were a ghost.
